  "notes": [
    "Exact byte sizes and paths verified through the official GitHub tree API on 2026-09-10; no sample audio downloaded for this manifest.",
    "Pitched sample filenames use C3=60, an octave below scientific pitch notation. root_midi follows the official SFZ mappings, not filename assumptions.",
    "velocity is a representative MIDI velocity for renderer layer choice; velocity_layer is the original source filename layer index. Dynamics still need musical gain/envelope control.",
    "Cello and viola sustains have two recorded dynamic layers; cello spiccato has two recorded dynamic layers and two round robins. Horn sustain subset favors quiet and medium layers.",
    "Sustain audio duration, sample rate and RIFF loop data were not inspected; read them after downloading. Official sustain SFZ files do not specify external loop points. Do not invent a tight sustain loop; use the natural recording for short notes or a carefully crossfaded long segment if needed.",
    "Cello root pitches 50,53,57 cover D3-A3; viola roots 59,62,65,69,72,76 cover the D4-D5 melody with at most two semitones of nearest-note transposition.",
    "Horn source has a genuine gap between MIDI 60 and 74. Prefer horn writing at MIDI 50-63; notes 64-70 require 4-7 semitones of transposition and may change character. Use viola for the upper melody or audition that range explicitly.",
    "Unpitched percussion root_midi is null and should play at original recorded pitch. The two cymbals are medium crashes with two round robins; no repeating bright mallet instruments are included.",
    "These are individual-note instrument recordings, not composed loops. The renderer must supply score, expressive envelopes, phrasing, mix and transitions."
  ],
